1
00:00:08,736 --> 00:00:12,556
This film is for teachers and lecturers.

2
00:00:12,616 --> 00:00:22,063
It shows board mode, where a whole class plays one experiment together, and its helper, ArdenBot.

3
00:00:22,773 --> 00:00:28,513
ArdenBot is Arden, together with a robot cat who gives him ideas.

4
00:00:28,573 --> 00:00:39,773
He sits in the panel under the board: he introduces the experiment, calls the turns and the points, and runs the vote and the questions.

5
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:48,504
His picture was made from a photo of Arden, used with his parent’s permission.

6
00:00:49,214 --> 00:00:54,644
Board mode hides the menus and makes text and buttons bigger.

7
00:00:54,704 --> 00:01:00,707
ArdenBot welcomes the class, and the discussion timer starts.

8
00:01:01,417 --> 00:01:11,777
Team Red tries 45 degrees; ArdenBot reads out the result and asks: will the next measurement go up, stay the same or go down?

9
00:01:11,837 --> 00:01:23,080
The teacher counts the raised hands on the board, no phones needed. The majority becomes the class prediction.

10
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:28,990
Team Blue changes the angle, tests it and hits the target.

11
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:37,317
A correct class prediction earns the team 1 point; hitting the target earns 3.

12
00:01:38,027 --> 00:01:44,767
The discussion question fits the stage of the experiment and starts the timer.

13
00:01:44,827 --> 00:01:51,554
When time is up, ArdenBot suggests collecting the ideas.

14
00:01:52,264 --> 00:01:59,234
The card gathers team points, tries, correct class predictions and solved levels.

15
00:01:59,294 --> 00:02:07,826
An optional class photo is processed only on the device; it never goes to the server.

16
00:02:08,536 --> 00:02:14,656
Split the class into one to four teams and choose the discussion time.

17
00:02:14,716 --> 00:02:22,226
Some games give ArdenBot their own class guide: team roles and questions for each stage.

18
00:02:22,286 --> 00:02:30,198
After a missed try, ArdenBot treats it as data and adds a question.

19
00:02:30,908 --> 00:02:38,498
ArdenBot is rule-based: it uses no language model and sends no questions to the internet.

20
00:02:38,558 --> 00:02:50,068
What he says comes from the anonymous state of the experiment: the number of tries, whether the target was hit, whether the prediction held.

21
00:02:50,128 --> 00:02:58,673
Votes and points stay in that browser tab and are deleted when it closes.

22
00:02:59,383 --> 00:03:06,433
Open it from the teacher menu in the game header, or add board=1 to the game link.

23
00:03:06,493 --> 00:03:14,944
Every lesson plan has a link that opens the game straight in board mode.

